# PACKAGING SYSTEM

Packaging is an extension of the archive.

It should feel permanent, intentional, and collectible.

The experience should resemble receiving an artifact rather than a product.

---

## PACKAGING PHILOSOPHY

Minimal.

Quiet.

Timeless.

Archival.

The packaging must support the concept without competing with it.

---

## MASTER BOX

Type

Rigid Premium Box

Finish

Matte

Color

Deep Matt Black

Construction

Clean Geometry

Minimal Exterior

No excessive decoration

---

## BOX BRANDING

Primary Mark

RARO MARK

Placement

Centered

Subtle

Single Color Application

Preferred Color

Antique Gold

No collection symbols on the exterior box.

The box represents the archive.

Not the individual collection.

---

## HANG TAG

Material

Heavyweight Premium Cardstock

Finish

Matte

Shape

Simple Geometric Form

Rounded or Sharp Corners Accepted

No decorative cuts

---

## HANG TAG STRUCTURE

Front

RARO MARK

Back

Collection Name

Edition Number

Example

VOID

01/40

or

ROOTS

03/40

---

## INTERNAL PRESENTATION

Garment folded cleanly.

Protected by archival tissue paper.

Minimal printed elements.

No promotional inserts.

No excessive messaging.

---

## LABELING PRINCIPLES

The archive comes first.

Collection comes second.

Branding should feel discovered rather than announced.

---

## COLOR APPLICATION

Exterior Box

Deep Black

RARO Mark

Antique Gold

Collection Information

Collection Print Color

Examples

VOID → Stone White

ROOTS → Off White

NHR → Muted Gold

DIJLA → Off White

ATHAR → Warm Sand

ECHO → Dark Gold

---

## PACKAGING MOOD

Museum Archive

Collected Artifact

Contemporary Object

Quiet Luxury

Timeless Design

---

## FORBIDDEN

Glossy Finishes

Bright Colors

Large Logos

Marketing Slogans

Crowded Layouts

Trend-Based Graphics

Plastic Visual Language

Luxury Through Simplicity
